From 78e4fadd010f72c3177a257acc89b0311a2d2463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 06:41:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UI: page-stack races around consent, discovery and Settings;
 Wormhole switch

Review findings kept[4], kept[5], kept[21], kept[22], kept[38] and the UI
half of kept[37]:

- Settings are saved when the page is left (its destruction), not on every
  Deactivating: the consent dialog pushed over Settings no longer sends
  set_settings, which restarted the receivers and withdrew the very offer
  shown, and committed half-typed values (F-C2, F-LS4).
- Discovery is counted in Engine.qml: a share that replaces an open Send
  page no longer has the old page's late stop_discovery empty the peer
  lists and stop discovery under the new page (F-LS1, F-QS1, F-C6).
- A send's or a wormhole code's reply leaves only its own page, only from
  the top of the stack, and otherwise once that page is Active again: it
  no longer pops or replaces a consent dialog that came up meanwhile,
  declining that offer unanswered (F-C2, S5).
- The window lets the next consent dialog in only once the last one has
  left the stack (its destruction), the dialog's closer keeps trying
  until it can leave instead of giving up, a dismissed dialog accepts
  nothing, and Engine.answer sends nothing for an offer that no longer
  waits: a closed offer's dialog can no longer stay stranded under the
  next one with a frozen countdown (F-C2, F-C3).
- Magic Wormhole can be switched off in Settings (settings.wormhole.enabled,
  default true, which the engine adds): it leaves the Send page and the
  main page's "Receive with a code" (F-C1). Translated in en, fi, de, sv.
- The Bluetooth nudge's Settings text now says what it does: while the
  Send page looks for devices it makes Android phones nearby show up
  (F-QS2). M-31 is rewritten to isolate the nudge (off, then on, with
  Android's Quick Share closed, both results recorded); M-16 covers F-C1,
  M-17 and M-6 check the page lifecycle on the phone.

Tests: tst_stack.qml (new, the whole window) reproduces each race;
tst_settings, tst_send and tst_engine cover the save-on-leave, the switch,
the discovery count and the answer refusal. Eight new selftest faults,
one per guard, are each caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ENZSCiAud5Vs29ugEacpyR
